.TH FERROKEYD.YAML 5 "August 2026" "Ferrokey" "Ferrokey Manual"
.SH NAME
ferrokeyd.yaml \- Ferrokey broker security-boundary configuration
.SH DESCRIPTION
Security-boundary configuration for
.BR ferrokeyd (1).
This file is the authorization and hardening policy of the privileged
supervisor; it must be owned by root and mode 0644
.RB ( "install \-m 0644 ferrokeyd.yaml /etc/ferrokey/ferrokeyd.yaml" ).
A user-writable config loaded by the privileged supervisor is refused.
.PP
Every field is optional; missing fields fall back to the defaults below.
Values are validated against hard bounds at load time.
.SH FIELDS
.TP
.B socket_path
Type: string (path). Default: "/run/ferrokeyd/ferrokeyd.sock". The AF_UNIX
socket the broker listens on. Validation: non-empty, at most 107 bytes; the
parent directory must exist, be owned by the service user, and not be
group/world-writable.
.TP
.B socket_mode
Type: octal integer. Default: 0666. The socket mode applied after creation.
0666 lets the unprivileged desktop UI connect; the real authority is the
SO_PEERCRED whitelist. Validation: at most 0777.
.TP
.B allowed_uids
Type: list of integers. Default: [] (deny-all). UIDs allowed to connect,
verified by the kernel via SO_PEERCRED; never supplied by the client.
.TP
.B allowed_gids
Type: list of integers. Default: []. GIDs allowed to connect.
.TP
.B max_connections
Type: integer. Default: 1. Maximum concurrent client connections.
Validation: 1..64.
.TP
.B rate
Type: map. Token-bucket rate limiting applied before any expensive work.
.RS
.TP
.B rate.burst
integer, default 200: maximum burst of messages.
.TP
.B rate.per_second
integer, default 200: sustained messages per second.
.RE
.RS
Validation: 1..10000.
.RE
.TP
.B max_held_keys
Type: integer. Default: 16. Maximum simultaneously-held keys on the virtual
device. Validation: 1..32.
.TP
.B device_name
Type: string. Default: "Ferrokey Virtual Keyboard". The name reported by
the virtual keyboard device. ABI-like: fixed at startup, never
client-controlled. Validation: at most 79 bytes.
.TP
.B service_user ", " service_group
Type: string. Defaults: "ferrokeyd". The dedicated unprivileged identity
the runtime broker drops to (groups, then gid, then uid, before the
freeze). The supervisor must be privileged enough to setuid/setgid to these
values.
.TP
.B session_scope
Type: string or null. Default: null (UID/GID-only authorization, the
Phase-3 baseline). Optional logind session-scope binding: when set, a
client is authorized only if its cgroup carries the SAME session scope. The
value is the cgroup scope name (form
.IR session-N.scope );
the number is assigned by the session manager at login and is
deployment-specific \- do not hard-code it in static configs (dynamic
session discovery is planned packaging work). Validation: strictly the form
.IR session-\fIdigits\fP.scope ,
no path syntax.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
    socket_path: /run/ferrokeyd/ferrokeyd.sock
    socket_mode: 438       # 0o666
    allowed_uids: [1000]
    allowed_gids: []
    max_connections: 1
    rate:
      burst: 200
      per_second: 200
    max_held_keys: 16
    device_name: "Ferrokey Virtual Keyboard"
    service_user: ferrokeyd
    service_group: ferrokeyd
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ferrokeyd (1),
.BR ferrokey.yaml (5),
.BR ferrokey (1)
